From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Read the H.26x pixel aspect when the input did not declare one

MediaCodec requests an opaque output before parsing its codec configuration.
An input with dimensions but no declared SAR starts that output at 1:1.
The decoded output format does not supply a replacement SAR. Use the H.26x
helper's current SPS when updating the output, while preserving any aspect
ratio declared by the container. This also avoids depending on a decoder
restart when the packetizer later discovers the same picture dimensions.
---
diff --git a/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c b/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
--- a/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
+++ b/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
@@ -455,6 +455,21 @@ static int UpdateVout(decoder_t *p_dec)
         p_dec->fmt_out.video.i_sar_den =
             p_sys->video.i_mpeg_dar_den * p_dec->fmt_out.video.i_width;
     }
+    else if ((p_dec->fmt_in.i_codec == VLC_CODEC_H264 ||
+              p_dec->fmt_in.i_codec == VLC_CODEC_HEVC) &&
+             (!p_dec->fmt_in.video.i_sar_num || !p_dec->fmt_in.video.i_sar_den))
+    {
+        /* The opaque output is created before codec extra data is parsed.
+         * MediaCodec's output format omits SAR; fill an undeclared aspect
+         * from the current SPS once that configuration is available. */
+        int num, den;
+        if (hxxx_helper_get_current_sar(&p_sys->video.hh, &num, &den) == VLC_SUCCESS
+         && num > 0 && den > 0)
+        {
+            p_dec->fmt_out.video.i_sar_num = num;
+            p_dec->fmt_out.video.i_sar_den = den;
+        }
+    }
 
     /* If MediaCodec can handle the rotation, reset the orientation to
      * Normal in order to ask the vout not to rotate. */
